 # ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
+# elabrows -- a BOOLEAN GENERIC ARM THAT NO SYNTHESISER HAS EVER BEEN GIVEN.
+# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
+# MEASURED 2026-09-20 by TRACK HDRCOST: `SCORE_HDR_TREE=1` had passed a
+# 20-point bit-exact grid against two C oracles, a 23-row mutation suite with
+# attribution controls, and five green gate groups -- and the first Vivado ever
+# aimed at it killed synth_design in 49 s on `[Synth 8-11324] array index 8 out
+# of range`.  GHDL evaluates the branch a run takes; Vivado unrolls the loop and
+# folds every index.  No bench in this repository can see that class of defect.
+#
+# THIS ROW DOES NOT RUN VIVADO AND CANNOT FIND SUCH A DEFECT.  It finds the
+# thing that let that one survive: an ABSENCE.  It recomputes the boolean-arm
+# census from the RTL and fails when a reachable arm no synthesiser has been
+# given is neither in `sim/elab_check_run.sh`'s row table nor in that script's
+# EXEMPT list with a written reason.  So a new lever turns the gate red until
+# someone schedules an elaboration row or writes down why it needs none.
+#
+# The Vivado half is `sim/elab_check_run.sh` and belongs pre-build and nightly,
+# NOT here: MEASURED, its three `fk33_llama_top` rows cost 758 s each and a
+# DERIVED 34.7 GB footprint.  This row costs 0.25 s and 12 MB.
+#
+# Teeth are in docs/debugging/2026-09-20_the-defect-only-a-synthesiser-sees.md
+# section 5.6: M1 a new one-armed generic, M2 a deleted elaboration row, M3 a
+# deleted exemption -- all KILLED; M4 a stale exemption and M5 a row whose top
+# does not build the generic it names -- both SURVIVE, and are the check's
+# stated resolution floor.
+printf 'elabrows\tsim\tRUN\t-\t-\t-\t-\n' >> "$PLAN"
+
+# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
 # gdnstale -- rtl/ooc_gdnadapt_top.vhd is GENERATED from rtl/llama_top.vhd by
 # sim/ooc_gdnadapt_extract.py, and it was STALE for two days.
 #
